    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 26 tests pass, including the three that target the new behavior (cp09, cp14, cp16).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and rebuilt everything derived from it.\n\n**Core logic** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the owners already in that city (counted case-insensitively via `findAll()`, mirroring the existing `CountNamesakes` pattern). This replaced the old global `findAll().size() + 1`.\n\nThe step still runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't counted among the existing city owners \u2014 giving consecutive numbers for same-city creates (verified by cp09).\n\n**Derived values** \u2014 `membershipNumber` (`AssignMembershipNumber`) reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` and appends `-M<YY>`, so it automatically rebuilds onto the new city-prefixed code; no logic change was needed there, just an updated Javadoc example. cp14 confirms `membershipNumber == customerCode + \"-M\" + YY`.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the Javadoc on both function classes and the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples in `openapi.yml` (`SYD-SMI-0007` / `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). The DB columns (`customer_code VARCHAR(20)`, `membership_number VARCHAR(32)`) already fit the longer format.\n\nNo YAML wiring changes were needed \u2014 the pipeline order in `owners.POST.yml` (`assignCustomerCode \u2192 assignMembershipNumber`) was already correct.",
